# nr-office-ooxml-pptx-base: integration fragment

mixdog-ooxml gets eight more modules (the pptx base of the portable engine): slide_shapes, pptx_targets, pptx_package,
pptx_core, pptx_chart, snapshot_shared, image_layout, review_editability. No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING
name belongs to this task. No Cargo dependency, workspace member or Cargo.lock edge is added: every module uses crates the
package already lists (mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, serde_json).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

Several ooxml tasks of the wave add modules to this file, so the lines are applied by the lead. In the module list, in
alphabetical order, add:

    pub mod image_layout;
    pub mod pptx_chart;
    pub mod pptx_core;
    pub mod pptx_package;
    pub mod pptx_targets;
    pub mod review_editability;
    pub mod slide_shapes;
    pub mod snapshot_shared;

In the crate documentation ("This part: ...") add after the placeholder scan / document fingerprint sentence: the slide shape
builders ([`slide_shapes`]), the presentation package ([`pptx_package`]), the slide reader and editor ([`pptx_core`]), the
operation targets ([`pptx_targets`]), the chart reader ([`pptx_chart`]), the helpers the format snapshots share
([`snapshot_shared`]), the picture layout ([`image_layout`]) and the editability review ([`review_editability`]).

The modules read each other as the Node files do: snapshot_shared reads pptx_chart, which reads pptx_package; pptx_core reads
pptx_package, relations and opc; review_editability reads relations; pptx_targets reads pptx_package and relations. None of
them reads a module another task of the wave adds.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-pipeline (keep the list sorted by set name), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-pptx-base.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-pptx-base/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "0139488a6bc46c013ff235fd2d2de07c6b5392dac1df546519ba504b4a69526f",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-pptx-base.mjs",
      "set": "office-pptx-base",
      "totalBytes": 485683
    }

The recording was made with --tree C:/Project/mixdog (the Node product at its working state; the eight source files are
byte-equal to the copy under D:/mixdog-build/mig/ref/node). The twin test is
crates/mixdog-ooxml/tests/twin_pptx_base.rs; nothing was compiled or run by this task.
